    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772-a1">

                <pb facs="0888" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg808"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr.
                            Naugle, assistant general manager Sonora
                        Railway.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-20"><hi rendition="#italic">March 20,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>. I write to inquire what has become of the
                    case of N. F. Bonsall.</p>
                <p>Kindly inform me whether the case has been disposed of, and, if not, what is its
                    present status.</p>
                <pb facs="0889" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/>
                <p>I have not heard from Mr. Bonsall since December 28 last, when he stated that he
                    would advise me if anything came up whereby I could assist him. Respectfully,
                    yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
